  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "IMREAL truncates complex text coefficients to 15 significant digits before returning binary64",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMREAL(inumber) parses complex text through Excel's 15-significant-digit decimal parser and flushes subnormal parsed coefficients below DBL_MIN to 0. Thus IMREAL(\"-1.5707963267948966\") returns -1.5707963267949 (0xbff921fb54442cfa) instead of 0xbff921fb54442d18. All 1,209 full-bank IMREAL rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (jnt_parity_complex rows 462-466, 592) and CalcFunc-Evidence cache/w111-extended-regenerated-20260929/answers-imreal.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430); 1,209/1,209 full-bank rows match.",
